# Admin guided tutorials — copy and presentation

## Objective

Driver.js tours in the admin help FAB must **teach**, not only point at controls. Staff should understand **why** a step exists and how it fits the academic model before acting.

## Mandatory copy standards

1. **Explain hierarchy and prerequisites** — When a tour touches nested entities (cohort → section → course), the **first step** (or intro popover) must state that the parent container must exist first. For this product, a **cohort is annual** (one per school year); **shifts** (morning, afternoon, etc.) belong in **sections**, not in separate cohorts. Example: sections and courses live **inside** the year’s cohort; create that cohort before adding sections.
2. **Substantive step descriptions** — Each step `description` in `dashboard.adminHelpTours.*.steps` should be **2–4 sentences** for conceptual steps (intro, hub, detail) and **at least 1–2 sentences** for mechanical steps (click Next, fill a field). Say what the control does, what happens next, and any common mistake to avoid.
3. **Catalog list blurbs** — `dashboard.adminHelpCatalog.<id>.description` should summarize the learning outcome (not only “guided walkthrough”).
4. **i18n** — Add or change keys in **`en.json`**, **`es.json`**, and **`pt.json`** together (**`09-i18n-copy.mdc`**). No user-visible literals in tour runners or help components.
5. **Duplicate-year guard** — Before opening the new-cohort modal, detect an existing cohort for the calendar year and show an **in-tour** Driver popover step with two footer actions (continue with existing vs create another). Copy lives in `dashboard.adminHelpTours.*.existingCohortPrompt` with `{{year}}` and `{{name}}` placeholders. Do not use a separate admin modal for this branch. Custom branch buttons must **not** use Driver’s `driver-popover-next-btn` / `driver-popover-footer-btn` classes — Driver.js delegates those clicks to `onNextClick` and will swallow the action.
6. **Tour stacking** — While Driver.js is active, modals opened during the tour use `stackBelowTour` (`show()` + `ge-modal-stacked`) so the tour popover stays above native top-layer dialogs. Activate the tour session **before** opening the modal so the first paint uses `show()`, never `showModal()`. `Modal` must derive stacked presentation from props (no delayed state that briefly opens top-layer). When the tour ends (**Listo** / Done), promote to `showModal()` **without** firing `onOpenChange(false)` — suppress the synthetic `close` from remount so the create form stays open for the real submit. For **create-new** from the year branch, close the branch tour first, then `openNewCohortModalForTutorial()` (session + stacked), then the modal step tour.
7. **Line breaks** — Use `\n\n` in dictionary descriptions for paragraphs; popover CSS uses `white-space: pre-line` on `.driver-popover-description`.

## Icons

1. **Tutorial list (React)** — Each `CATALOG` row declares an `icon` key; render a leading **Lucide** icon (`h-4 w-4`, `aria-hidden`) beside the title in `AdminHelpTutorialList` (**`16-admin-buttons-icons.mdc`**).
2. **Tour step titles (Driver popover)** — Prefix titles with a **single Unicode symbol** in dictionaries (e.g. 📚, ➕) when it aids scanning; keep the rest of the title human-readable for screen readers.
3. **Help panel chrome** — Prefer Lucide on headings/actions where space allows (e.g. `CircleHelp` in panel header).

Do not add a second icon library for tutorials.

## Architecture checklist (new tour)

- [ ] `catalog.ts` — id, `catalogKey`, `icon` (task tutorials)
- [ ] Pure step builder under `src/lib/admin-tutorials/`
- [ ] Intro step when domain concepts need context (`anchor: null` welcome popover)
- [ ] `adminHelpCatalog` + `adminHelpTours` keys in all locales
- [ ] `startAdminTutorial` switch case
- [ ] Vitest for step order / copy wiring
- [ ] **`listTourRuntimeChecks` row** (`task:<id>` or `screen:<id>`) so L3 `@admin-tours` covers the tour — see **`33-admin-tutorials-contract.mdc`**
- [ ] Update inventory / L1 contracts when anchors/routes change
- [ ] Analytics unchanged or extended per **`08-analytics-observability.mdc`**

## Screen explain tours (contextual FAB)

- Always show **Explain this screen** first in the help panel (`AdminHelpExplainScreenBlock`).
- Register routes in `screenCatalog.ts` (`resolveAdminScreenTour`).
- **Admin home** (`admin-home`) is the **only** tour with scope `chrome-and-content` (sidebar + header + content).
- All **future** screen tours must use scope `content-only` — do not re-highlight nav/chrome.
- Copy under `dashboard.adminHelpExplainScreen` + `dashboard.adminHelpScreenTours.<id>`.
- Runner: `startExplainScreenTour`; entity prefix `admin_screen_tour:*`.

